    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d32">

                <pb facs="0049" n="37" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg37"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.20290H/7: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Afghanistan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kabul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-05-27T22:00:00+04:00">May 27, 1943—10
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 28 (?)—4:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>110. My 107, May 24, noon. British Minister saw Afghan Prime Minister last night
                    and tells me interview was rather stormy. Premier requested one week to consider
                    his reply and Sir Francis agreed.</p>
                <p>Foreign Minister<anchor n="44" xml:id="d32-f1"/> admits that Bokharan refugees
                    arrested had been in touch with Axis Legations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d32-f1" n="44" xml:id="d32-f1-content">
                <p>Ali Mohamed Khan.</p>
            </note>
